+Normalize surrounding whitespace and uppercase ASCII letters before lookup. Serial-number punctuation remains significant. Return the snapshot date even when no matching record exists. Lookups query the local SQLite index; the query path is a prepared statement against a normalized serial column with an index for sub-250 ms resolution on 90,000 records.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Lookup backend | Local embedded SQLite index | On-site HTTPS directory; Managed search service | Predictable local lookups with no service to run; each kiosk validates and rebuilds its own index when a snapshot arrives; stays inside registry component; aligns with HLD tenets prohibiting runtime network access. |
+| Index rebuild strategy | Atomic rebuild to new database file then swap | In-place updates | Guarantees no partially imported snapshot is visible; import failure leaves previous snapshot active. |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+### Resolved
+1. ✅ Lookup backend selected as local embedded SQLite index.
+
+### Deferred
+1. SQLite schema versioning and migration path for future schema changes.
+2. Storage location and backup of the SQLite file on kiosk.
